A||||5||Banzai||Crazy blinkers||||1||
Z||000000||Banzai||12-11-2001||06:50 AM||||The blinkers on my 84 are acting strange.  When I first got it on the road the right side lights would come on but wouldn't flash the left side worked normally. I replaced the bulbs and still no change so I replaced the flasher. Now the right side flashes normally and the left side flashes super fast.Help<P>Banzai !!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||tesmith66||12-11-2001||07:14 AM||||Check ALL your grounds. Make sure every light has a good ground, and make sure the battery is grounded to the engine, and the engine is gounded to the chassis.<P>------------------<BR>Timothy E. Smith<BR>1986 SE V6<BR>1984 Coupe||||reg||1
Z||000002||JohnF||12-11-2001||08:09 AM||||Crazy blinkers on one side usually indicate a problem with the marker light on that side, (front or rear or both), not the blinkers themselves.  Check bulbs, grounds, power to those.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001107&p=57211671&Sequence=0"> <BR>You can have all the SPEED you can afford!||||reg||1
Z||000003||GTDude||12-11-2001||09:03 AM||||Definitely check bulbs and grounds first, but I've also seen the turn signal switch cause this problem.  So suspect this if you can find no other probs.<P>GTDude<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||NEPTUNE||12-11-2001||09:13 AM||||Hope those suggestions help. If nothing else works you could move to Florida where signals seem to be prohibited.||||reg||6
Z||000005||Banzai||12-12-2001||08:12 PM||||Thanks all I'll check out all the grounds and sockets. Before, while I was checking the lights I found two of the markers had slightly corroded contacts. <P>Banzai !!!!!||||reg||1
